From ebb28c5eea201d68eef9521bd7de37cb5e1d58c2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TB710FU clean board <tb710fu@localhost>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 05:20:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Trace kalloc initialization boundaries

Reason: the existing completion-only marker cannot identify which operation follows the last recorded checkpoint. Pair events around each kalloc_init operation, instrument fixed/variable view phases, and emit bounded loop progress so one hardware capture covers the full ZALLOC callback.

Source: pinned XNU ac9718fb1af618d5ce8678d0dc6e8a58f252216f, after device patch 0018. Diagnostics are active only with the selected live-log provider; allocator policy, callback order, and memory operations are unchanged.

Verification: isolated pinned-XNU fixture passes git diff --check and balanced event-label audit. Native arm64e build, strict prelink, and production parser remain pending.
---
 osfmk/kern/kalloc.c | 170 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 158 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

